## How to run and rebuild

**First time / after changing Dockerfile or requirements.txt:**
```bash
docker compose build --no-cache
docker compose up
```

**Normal start:**
```bash
docker compose up
```

**Stop:**
```bash
docker compose down
```

**See live logs:**
```bash
docker compose logs -f
```

**Get a shell inside the running container (useful for debugging):**
```bash
docker exec -it python_container /bin/bash
```

---

## What each environment variable does

| Variable | Value | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `ENABLE_OCR` | `true` | Activates OCR for scanned PDFs. Leave unset to skip OCR (faster). |

---

## Common failure modes and what they mean

**`n8n error 404: webhook not registered`**
n8n's test webhook only activates when you have the workflow open in the browser and click "Execute workflow". For permanent use you need to switch the workflow to production mode (toggle from "Test" to "Active" in n8n) and update `WEBHOOK_URL` to use `/webhook/` instead of `/webhook-test/`.

**`⚠ No text content found — PDF may be a blank template or scanned without OCR enabled`**
Either `ENABLE_OCR` is not set to `true`, or the PDF is genuinely a blank template with nothing to read.

**`⚠ OCR ran but found no text`**
OCR ran but tesseract couldn't recognize anything. Usually means the scan quality is very poor (too dark, blurry, or very low resolution).

**`⚠ Target already exists`**
A file with the generated name already exists in the folder. The rename is skipped to avoid overwriting. You'll need to manually resolve the naming conflict.

**`✗ Request failed: ...`**
Python couldn't reach n8n at all. Check that both containers are on the same Docker network (`n8n_n8n-internal`) and that n8n is running.

---

## Things to be aware of (the "dangerous" part of vibe coding)

**No error recovery for failed renames.** If the rename fails halfway (e.g. disk full), the file stays with its original name and no retry happens. The log will show the error but nothing will fix it automatically.

**No queue.** If 10 files arrive at once, they're all processed simultaneously. This is usually fine but could cause issues under heavy load.

**The OCR parsing is tuned to one specific form** (Muster 4 Krankenbeförderung). Other form types will fall back to the generic "Dokument_date" naming. The `parse_patient_info` function would need extension to handle different layouts.

**The webhook URL is hardcoded.** If you change your n8n setup, you need to update `WEBHOOK_URL` in `watch_folder.py` and rebuild.

**Tesseract makes mistakes.** OCR is never 100% accurate, especially on handwritten or low-quality scans. Always sanity-check renamed files occasionally to catch misreadings.
